              "text": "ਥਾਪ (thāp) is inherited from a reconstructed thapp, \"slap, pat\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi thāp, \"pat, slap\", under it and marks it masculine (CDIAL 6091). CDIAL does not give the sense \"drumbeat\", and the feminine use taught here (the beat of the drum) is not recorded there."
